{"timestamp":"2026-08-31T08:57:40.621Z","ordinal":4882,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a05669-fc4c-7aa0-b9a1-034d833ed8ed","turn_id":"01a05707-953f-7740-b541-b3122741c3a1","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-e56e39d7-072f-415a-9e39-c86eaa1ee976","process_id":"95452","command":["/bin/bash","-lc","docker exec tiered-serve bash -lc \"cd /root/projects/tiered-serve && sed -n '1,760p' tiered_serve/dietgpu_kv_compressor.py\""],"cwd":"file:///home/ubuntu","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"docker exec tiered-serve bash -lc \"cd /root/projects/tiered-serve && sed -n '1,760p' tiered_serve/dietgpu_kv_compressor.py\""}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"\"\"\"DietGPU KV cache compressor.\n\nProvides a drop-in replacement for ``ZipServCompressor`` when used as the\n``kv_compressor`` in ``DualMemoryLoader``.  Uses the DietGPU raw ANS codec\n(exponent-only compression + raw sign|mantissa storage) for BF16 KV cache\nblocks.\n\nInterface parity with ZipServCompressor's KV methods (the subset that is\nexercised from ``DualMemoryLoader``, ``kv_offload_system`` and\n``v1_cuda_graph_wrapper``):\n\n- ``batch_decomp_stream`` attribute\n- ``warmup_kv_buffers(block_shape, max_n_blocks, n_layers, ...)``\n- ``init_kv_compress_workers(n_workers, max_blocks, n_layers)``\n- ``compress_batch_async(layer_id, block_ids, gpu_k, gpu_v)``\n- ``wait_compress_async(layer_id, block_shape, timeout_sec)``\n- ``stop_kv_compress_workers()``\n- ``has_compressed_kv(layer_id)`` / ``_compressed_kv`` dict\n- ``has_persistent_compressed_kv(layer_id, block_ids)``\n- ``decompress_batch(layer_id, block_ids, output_buffers=(k_cache, v_cache))``\n- ``free_persistent_block(layer_id, block_id)``\n\nUnlike ZipServ, there is no C++ worker thread pool — DietGPU compresses\nentirely on GPU, so ``compress_batch_async`` simply launches the\ncompress + D2H pipeline on an internal CUDA stream and ``wait_compress_async``\nsynchronises it.\n\nStorage layout (per layer, per K and V):\n  - ``comp_exp`` : pinned [max_n_blocks, max_comp_size] uint8 row-major by\n    physical slot.  Actual per-block payload length tracked in ``exp_sizes``.\n  - ``sm``       : pinned [max_n_blocks, block_bytes] uint8 row-major by\n    physical slot.\n  - ``exp_sizes``: pinned [max_n_blocks] int32 — per-slot compressed size.\n  - ``_kv_slot`` : block_id -> physical slot.  Slots [0, active_count) are\n    kept dense via eager swap-with-last on free.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport logging\nimport os\nfrom typing import Any, Dict, List, Optional, Tuple\n\nimport numpy as np\nimport torch\n\nfrom tiered_serve.compressor_base import TensorCompressor\nfrom tiered_serve.tensor_compressor import _ensure_dietgpu_loaded\n\nlogger = logging.getLogger(__name__)\n\n\n# DietGPU ANS worst-case compressed size for a batch of equal-size inputs.\n# Mirrors ``getMaxCompressedSize`` from dietgpu/ans/GpuANSEncode.cu which is\n# roughly ``overhead + max_block_size_coalesced * ceil(N / 4096)`` where each\n# 4096-byte block can expand to ~2x of its input in the coalesced layout.\n# Use a conservative bound of ``2 * N + 16 KiB`` rounded to 128 B.\ndef _max_comp_size(uncompressed_bytes: int) -> int:\n    size = uncompressed_bytes * 2 + 16 * 1024\n    return (size + 127) & ~127\n\n\nclass DietGPUKVCompressor(TensorCompressor):\n    \"\"\"DietGPU-based KV cache compressor.\n\n    Inherits :class:`TensorCompressor` so that\n    :class:`tiered_serve.dual_memory_loader.DualMemoryLoader` can hold\n    ``weight_compressor`` and ``kv_compressor`` as uniformly-typed\n    :class:`TensorCompressor` instances.\n\n    The single-tensor weight API (``compress`` / ``decompress`` /\n    ``compress_batch`` / ``decompress_batch``) is **not** implemented —\n    this backend is KV-only and exposes its work through KV-specific\n    batch methods (``compress_batch_async`` / ``wait_compress_async`` /\n    ``decompress_batch``).  Calls to the weight API raise\n    :class:`NotImplementedError`.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, comp_stream: torch.cuda.Stream,\n                 workspace_bytes: int = 384 * 1024 * 1024):\n        _ensure_dietgpu_loaded()\n        # TensorCompressor.__init__ sets up comp_stream/decomp_stream\n        # defaults; we overwrite comp_stream below with the caller's.\n        super().__init__(comp_stream=comp_stream)\n        self.comp_stream = comp_stream\n        self.batch_decomp_stream = torch.cuda.Stream(priority=0)\n        self._workspace = torch.empty(\n            [workspace_bytes], dtype=torch.uint8, device=\"cuda\")\n\n        # Per-layer transient state populated by ``compress_batch_async``\n        # and committed by ``wait_compress_async`` so downstream readers\n        # (e.g. DualMemoryLoader's persistent decompress path) can see\n        # which buffer_ids were just written into the host pool.\n        self._compressed_kv: Dict[int, Any] = {}\n\n        # Persistent compressed store bookkeeping.\n        # ``_persistent_valid[layer_id]`` is a bytearray of length max_n_blocks\n        # where 1 means \"this block has compressed data in the host pool\".\n        self._persistent_valid: Dict[int, bytearray] = {}\n        # Per-layer compressed-row slot mapping.  Unlike the logical vLLM block\n        # id, physical slots are compacted eagerly on free so the host store\n        # remains a dense prefix.\n        self._kv_slot: Dict[int, torch.Tensor] = {}\n        self._kv_slot_block: Dict[int, List[int]] = {}\n        self._kv_active_count: Dict[int, int] = {}\n\n        self._kv_pools_ready = False\n        # Per-layer host pools: {layer_id: {'k': pool_dict, 'v': pool_dict}}\n        self._host_pools: Dict[int, Dict[str, Dict[str, torch.Tensor]]] = {}\n        # GPU staging pools for compress output (shared across layers):\n        # {'k': ..., 'v': ...} each with comp_exp[N,S] uint8, sm[N,B] uint8,\n        # sizes[N] int32\n        self._gpu_comp_pool: Dict[str, Dict[str, torch.Tensor]] = {}\n        # GPU staging pools for decompress input\n        self._gpu_decomp_pool: Dict[str, Dict[str, torch.Tensor]] = {}\n\n        self._block_numel: int = 0              # elements per block (BF16)\n        self._block_bytes: int = 0              # bytes per block (uint8 view)\n        self._max_comp_size: int = 0            # per-block compressed stride\n        self._block_shape: Tuple[int, ...] = ()\n        self._max_n_blocks: int = 0\n        self._max_gpu_blocks: int = 0\n        self._max_gpu_decomp_blocks: int = 0\n        self._n_layers: int = 0\n\n        # Pending async compress state for wait_compress_async.\n        # {layer_id: {'event': CUDA event, 'buffer_ids': list, ...}}\n        self._pending_compress: Dict[int, Dict[str, Any]] = {}\n\n    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n    #  Warmup\n    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n    def _compute_max_comp_size(self, block_bytes: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Worst-case compressed bytes for one ``block_bytes``-row.\n        Subclasses (e.g. MantExp with non-DietGPU codec) may override.\n        \"\"\"\n        _probe = torch.empty(block_bytes, dtype=torch.uint8, device='cuda')\n        _rows, mcs = torch.ops.dietgpu.max_any_compressed_output_size([_probe])\n        del _probe\n        return (int(mcs) + 127) & ~127\n\n    def warmup_kv_buffers(\n        self,\n        block_shape: tuple,\n        max_n_blocks: int,\n        n_layers: int = 1,\n        max_gpu_blocks: int = 0,\n        max_gpu_decomp_blocks: int = 0,\n        huge_page_allocator=None,\n        pre_allocated_host_pools=None,\n    ) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Pre-allocate flat per-block buffers for KV compress/decompress.\"\"\"\n        if max_gpu_blocks <= 0:\n            max_gpu_blocks = max_n_blocks\n        if max_gpu_decomp_blocks <= 0:\n            max_gpu_decomp_blocks = max_gpu_blocks\n\n        block_numel = 1\n        for s in block_shape:\n   